GIMP Palette
Name: Durham colour palette 2019 (accessible variants)
Columns: 5
#
# Durham's 2019 palette, plus darkened variants of the hues that fail WCAG
# contrast on white. Accessibility outranks exact brand adherence here: the
# figures are teaching material, projected in a lit room, and several
# students each year have a colour-vision deficiency.
#
# Ratios are against white, the figure background. WCAG 2.1 SC 1.4.11 asks
# 3:1 for graphical objects; the "AA" entries below target 4.5:1 instead,
# because a projector washes out the margin a monitor preserves, and the
# extra headroom lets the same colour serve as a text label.
#
# Variants darken in HSV, holding hue and saturation, so they read as the
# Durham hue rather than as a different colour.
#
0   0   0  True Black #000000
51 49 50 Black #333132
0 42 65 Ink #002A41
104 36 109 Purple #68246D
255 213 58 Yellow #FFD53A
0 174 239 Cyan #00AEEF
190 30 45 Red #BE1E2D
175 169 97 Gold #AFA961
203 168 177 Heather #CBA8B1
218 205 162 Stone #DACDA2
165 200 208 Sky #A5C8D0
182 170 167 Cedar #B6AAA7
179 189 177 Concrete #B3BDB1
255 255 255  White #ffffff
#
# Accessible variants. Originals fail on white at the ratio shown; each of
# these clears 4.5:1.
#
# Cyan 2.53, Gold 2.42, Yellow 1.42, Concrete 1.94
#
0 127 175 Cyan AA #007FAF
125 120 69 Gold AA #7D7845
139 116 32 Yellow AA #8B7420
114 120 113 Concrete AA #727871
